      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-304003",
      ":question/problem": "A survey conducted among a group of households determined whether they had high-speed internet and cable television. The results are shown in the table below.\n\n|  | Has cable TV | Does not have cable TV |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Has high-speed internet | $14$ | $6$ |\n| Does not have high-speed internet | $12$ | $8$ |\n\nIf one of these households is chosen at random, what is the probability that it has high-speed internet but does not have cable TV?"
